  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN.\n\nConsider the following steps:\n\n\nChoose an integer kkk (1≤k≤N)(1 \\leq k \\leq N)(1≤k≤N);\nDivide the range [1,N][1, N][1,N] into kkk intervals [li,ri][l_i,r_i][li​,ri​] (1≤i≤k)(1 \\leq i \\le k)(1≤i≤k) such that:\n\nl1=1l_1=1l1​=1 and rk=Nr_k=Nrk​=N;\nli+1=ri+1l_{i+1}=r_i+1li+1​=ri​+1 for all (1≤i&lt;k)(1 \\leq i \\lt k)(1≤i&lt;k).\n\n\nThe score of this split is defined as k−∑i=1kmax⁡(Ali,Ali+1,…,Ari)k-\\sum_{i=1}^k \\max(A_{l_i},A_{l_{i}+1},\\ldots,A_{r_i})k−∑i=1k​max(Ali​​,Ali​+1​,…,Ari​​).\nFind the **maximum** possible score of a split across all 1≤k≤N1 \\leq k \\leq N1≤k≤N.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN, the size of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **maximum** possible score of a split across all 1≤k≤N1 \\leq k \\leq N1≤k≤N.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 4⋅1054\\cdot 10^54⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n2 -2 2\n3\n5 -2 5\n4\n-1 -1 -1 -1\n8\n-7 -1 5 9 -1 -2 7 8",
        "output": "1\n-4\n8\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Choose k=3k=3k=3 and [l1,r1]=[1,1],[l2,r2]=[2,2],[l3,r3]=[3,3][l_1,r_1]=[1,1],[l_2,r_2]=[2,2],[l_3,r_3]=[3,3][l1​,r1​]=[1,1],[l2​,r2​]=[2,2],[l3​,r3​]=[3,3].\nThe score of this split is k−(max⁡(A1)+max⁡(A2)+max⁡(A3))=3−(2−2+2)=1k-(\\max(A_1)+\\max(A_2)+\\max(A_3))=3-(2-2+2)=1k−(max(A1​)+max(A2​)+max(A3​))=3−(2−2+2)=1. We can show that no other split for any kkk yields a score greater than −4-4−4.\nTest case 222: Choose k=1k=1k=1 and [l1,r1]=[1,3][l_1,r_1]=[1,3][l1​,r1​]=[1,3].\nThe score of this split is k−(max⁡(A1,A2,A3))=1−5=−4k-(\\max(A_1,A_2,A_3))=1-5=-4k−(max(A1​,A2​,A3​))=1−5=−4. We can show that no other split for any kkk yields a score greater than 111."
      }
    ]
